part.text:
Confirmed: `COMMIT` directly inside a block that has an `EXCEPTION` clause fails with "cannot commit while a subtransaction is active". So my plan for sp_monthly_report must use the nested structure:

```sql
BEGIN
    BEGIN
        ... work ...
    EXCEPTION
        WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN NULL;
        WHEN OTHERS THEN RAISE;
    END;
    COMMIT;
END;
```

That worked in probe C.

Note the shell exit code echoed 0 even on the psql error (because echo ran after psql... whatever, the ERROR output is clear).

Now probe D: custom exception with ERRCODE P0002 caught by WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND — in a procedure. And also test ROLLBACK inside an EXCEPTION handler (to know whether I could translate the Oracle ROLLBACK literally — likely same "subtransaction active" error).

input.command:
psql -X -d migtest <<'EOF'
-- Probe D: raise a custom exception tagged with the no-data SQLSTATE and
-- catch it by condition name; also test ROLLBACK inside a handler.
CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE probe_d() LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $proc$
DECLARE
    v_has_data numeric := 0;
BEGIN
    BEGIN
        SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_has_data;
        IF v_has_data = 0 THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION 'no data available for monthly report'
                USING ERRCODE = 'P0002';
        END IF;
        RAISE NOTICE 'D: normal path';
    EXCEPTION
        WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
            RAISE NOTICE 'D: caught no_data_found (SQLSTATE %)', SQLSTATE;
        WHEN OTHERS THEN
            RAISE NOTICE 'D: caught others (SQLSTATE %)', SQLSTATE;
    END;
END;
$proc$;

CALL probe_d();

-- Probe G: ROLLBACK inside an exception handler (literal translation attempt)
DO $do$
BEGIN
    BEGIN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'boom';
    EXCEPTION WHEN OTHERS THEN
        ROLLBACK;
    END;
END
$do$;
EOF

